{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4067d9d1b20fea521fd18b3433949ebfaa095ce8053b54ff31649b524580e5a8","digest":{"component_or_area":"editor-server test fixture","key_entities":["ThreadingHTTPServer","HTTPServer.server_bind","socket.getfqdn","TCPServer.server_bind","_LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer","src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py","tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py","edit_workflow","127.0.0.1"],"problem_keywords":["reverse DNS","loopback server","socket.getfqdn","HTTPServer construction","performance regression","test fixture latency"],"propositions":["socket.getfqdn called during HTTPServer.server_bind adds ~35 seconds of latency on macOS Verify runners when resolving numeric 127.0.0.1, blocking test fixture setup and violating test negligibility contract","The loopback editor-server fixture does not consume or assert on server_name, making the reverse-DNS lookup unnecessary for the test contract","A custom _LoopbackThreadingHTTPServer subclass that delegates to TCPServer.server_bind and derives server_name from the literal bound address eliminates the reverse-DNS call without changing editor workflow behavior","The fix preserves real loopback HTTP serving, ephemeral port selection, request handling, authentication, shutdown, and all existing test coverage while removing the 35-second long pole"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787352628479617001,"uuid":"9c6eca2e-d383-459c-9a4e-35fe1eb1591c"}